[# docs-src/repos/cx-binding-rust.cxd — the Rust binding's page,
   repo-cx-binding-rust.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 4).
   Facts from the registries; the one example from the front door's ABI
   vectors, the corpus every binding grades itself against. #]

[repo name=cx-binding-rust
  [intro
    """**TL;DR — the same C ABI, in the host's own idiom.** `cx-binding-rust`
       is the `cxlib` crate: a thin wrapper over `libcx`'s string-in,
       string-out C ABI, so a Rust program parses, canonicalises, hashes,
       converts and evaluates CX with the very engine the `cx` binary runs —
       byte-identical answers, nothing reimplemented."""]
  [body
    """Layer 1 is the contract every binding shares: sixteen canonical
       methods — parse, bytes, hash, equals, eval, select, modify and the
       node accessors — with identical semantics across hosts, so a document
       hashed from Rust is the document hashed from anywhere else. Identity
       rides `cx_canonical`, `cx_hash` and `cx_eq`; selection, evaluation and
       update delegate to `cx_code_eval`; nothing about a document is
       retained inside `libcx` between calls. [[layer-1]] is the table,
       [[c-abi]] the surface beneath it, [[layer-2]] the host-idiomatic
       sugar above it that desugars to Layer 1."""]
  [body
    """The front door publishes the ABI vectors every binding grades itself
       against — one case per entry point a wrapper covers, an input
       document and the canonical output, hash or refusal it must answer —
       and checks the same file against `libcx` directly in its C test. The
       crate's own lane over those vectors is owed: its repository's check
       grades the pins alone today, and its own build notes say so rather
       than dressing a skip as a pass."""]
  [gives
    """No CX module: a binding ships host code, not `.cx` files, so the table
       below is the generator's note. What it gives you is the crate itself —
       the Layer-1 methods, and the host-idiomatic layer above them that
       desugars to Layer 1."""]
  [try
    """One ABI vector, replayed by this site's `cx`: an XML document imported
       to CX through the entry point the wrapper's XML-to-CX call wraps, and
       the canonical text it must answer. A binding's lane asserts the same
       vector through its wrapper; this page shows the engine's own answer."""]
  [fixture id=abi-010-xml-to-cx]
  [status
    """The binding is not consumed by `cx` — it consumes `cx`: its own
       `deps.cxd` pins the front door for the C ABI and the V core it builds
       `libcx` from, which is why the registry row carries no `at=` and the
       figure draws no column on either side. It ships from its own
       repository at its own cadence, and a pin moves there only when the
       newer front door is green with it."""]]
